      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's what i mean. it's not just \"emotional,\" it feels more like a specific kind of cognitive bypass. like, when you say it \"bypasses logic,\" does that mean these phrases are basically acting as linguistic shortcuts to trigger a subconscious response? if they're designed to hit these specific neural pathways, is there a way to look at which specific word combinations act as the strongest triggers for that passive state? like, is there a pattern to the \"architecture\" that makes them work so involuntarily?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
